## How It Works

```
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│         YOUR PERSONAL TELEGRAM ACCOUNT           │
│            (Telethon Userbot Session)            │
└─────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┘
                      │ listens to new messages
        ┌─────────────▼──────────────┐
        │      42+ Source Groups     │
        │  (Uzbek groups in Korea)   │
        └─────────────┬──────────────┘
                      │
        ┌─────────────▼──────────────┐
        │         monitor.py         │
        │  1. Repost duplicate check │
        │  2. Two-tier keyword filter│
        │  3. Format message (KST)   │
        └─────────────┬──────────────┘
                      │ forwards
        ┌─────────────▼──────────────┐
        │   Korea Ish E'lonlari      │
        │     (Target Group)         │
        └────────────────────────────┘

        ┌────────────────────────────┐
        │     Admin Bot (aiogram)    │
        │  Manage groups, view stats │
        │  Test keywords, get alerts │
        └────────────────────────────┘
```

---

## Features

| # | Feature | Description |
|---|---------|-------------|
| 1 | **Personal account monitoring** | Uses Telethon to read messages from groups where bots cannot enter |
| 2 | **Two-tier keyword filter** | Tier 1: strong exact keywords. Tier 2: fuzzy word-combination matching for real-world messy writing |
| 3 | **Repost deduplication** | Same job post forwarded across multiple groups is only sent once |
| 4 | **KST timestamps** | All message times displayed in Korea Standard Time (UTC+9) |
| 5 | **Auto-delete join/leave messages** | Keeps the target group clean automatically |
| 6 | **No link preview cards** | "VIEW GROUP" / "VIEW USER" cards are suppressed |
| 7 | **Admin control panel** | Full Telegram bot UI to manage everything without touching code |
| 8 | **Group membership verification** | Warns you if the monitor account hasn't joined a newly added group |
| 9 | **Keyword tester** | Paste any message to see if the filter would catch it and why |
| 10 | **Analytics & stats** | 7-day statistics: top groups, language breakdown, detection method |
| 11 | **Error notifications** | Instant DM to admin if a message fails to send |
| 12 | **Daily summary at 9pm KST** | Automated evening report with today's forwarding stats |
| 13 | **SQLite database** | Lightweight persistent storage — no external database needed |

---

## Project Structure

```
telegram_job_bot/
│
├── bot/
│   ├── __init__.py       # Package marker
│   ├── admin_bot.py      # aiogram admin control panel bot
│   ├── client.py         # Shared Telethon client singleton
│   ├── config.py         # Environment variable loader
│   ├── database.py       # SQLite: groups, stats, dedup tables
│   ├── filters.py        # Two-tier keyword detection engine
│   ├── monitor.py        # Telethon userbot: listens & forwards
│   ├── notifier.py       # Admin error notification system
│   ├── scheduler.py      # Daily 9pm KST summary scheduler
│   └── utils.py          # Logging, HTML formatting, helpers
│
├── data/                 # Auto-created — SQLite database file
├── logs/                 # Auto-created — job_bot.log
├── sessions/             # Auto-created — Telethon session file
│
├── main.py               # ⭐ Unified entry point (recommended)
├── main_monitor.py       # Standalone monitor only
├── main_admin.py         # Standalone admin bot only
├── requirements.txt
├── .env.example
├── .gitignore
└── README.md
```

---

## Requirements

- **Python 3.11 or higher**
- A personal Telegram account
- Telegram API credentials (free)
- A Telegram Bot token (free, from @BotFather)

---

## Setup Guide

### Step 1 — Get Telegram API credentials

1. Go to **https://my.telegram.org/apps**
2. Log in with your phone number
3. Click **Create application**
4. Copy your `api_id` and `api_hash`

### Step 2 — Create an Admin Bot

1. Open Telegram and message **@BotFather**
2. Send `/newbot` and follow the prompts
3. Copy the **bot token** (looks like `123456789:ABCdef...`)

### Step 3 — Get your Telegram User ID

1. Message **@userinfobot** on Telegram
2. It replies with your numeric ID (e.g. `123456789`)

### Step 4 — Install Python dependencies

```bash
# Create a virtual environment (recommended)
python -m venv venv

# Activate it
source venv/bin/activate        # Linux / macOS
venv\Scripts\activate           # Windows

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### Step 5 — Configure environment variables

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

Open `.env` and fill in every value:

```env
API_ID=12345678
API_HASH=your_api_hash_here
PHONE_NUMBER=+998901234567
BOT_TOKEN=123456789:ABCdef...
ADMIN_USER_ID=987654321
TARGET_GROUP=KoreaIshElonlari
```

| Variable | Description | Example |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `API_ID` | Telegram API app ID | `12345678` |
| `API_HASH` | Telegram API app hash | `abc123def456...` |
| `PHONE_NUMBER` | Your account phone number | `+998901234567` |
| `BOT_TOKEN` | Admin bot token from @BotFather | `123:ABC...` |
| `ADMIN_USER_ID` | Your Telegram numeric user ID | `987654321` |
| `TARGET_GROUP` | Output group username or numeric ID | `KoreaIshElonlari` |

---

## Running the Bot

### ⭐ Recommended — run everything together

```bash
python main.py
```

This starts the monitor, admin bot, and daily scheduler in one process. On first run, Telegram will send a verification code to your phone — enter it in the terminal.

### Alternative — run separately (two terminals)

```bash
# Terminal 1: monitor
python main_monitor.py

# Terminal 2: admin bot
python main_admin.py
```

> ⚠️ When running separately, `@username` group resolution and the `🧪 Test Send` feature require both processes to be running together via `main.py`.

---

## Admin Bot Commands

Open Telegram and message your admin bot. All commands are also available as keyboard buttons.

| Button / Command | Description |
|-----------------|-------------|
| 📋 List Groups / `/listgroups` | Show all monitored source groups with ID, link, and date added |
| ➕ Add Group / `/addgroup` | Add a group by numeric ID or @username. Automatically resolves the real group name and checks membership |
| ➖ Remove Group / `/removegroup` | Tap-to-remove inline keyboard — no typing required |
| 🎯 Set Target / `/settarget` | Set the destination group where job posts are forwarded |
| 🔍 Test Keyword / `/testkeyword` | Paste any message text to see if the filter detects it as a job post |
| 📈 Stats / `/stats` | 7-day analytics: total forwarded, top source groups, language breakdown |
| 🧪 Test Send / `/test` | Send a test message to the target group to verify connectivity |
| 📊 Status / `/status` | Current monitor status, group list, and total messages forwarded |

### How to get a group's numeric ID

Forward any message from that group to **@userinfobot** — it will reply with the group's numeric ID (e.g. `-1001234567890`).

---

## Message Format

Every forwarded job post looks like this in the target group:

```
⚠️ New Message Information:

Group: xxxx          ← clickable, opens the group
Message Owner: xxxx              ← clickable, opens their profile
Message Time: 2026-03-06 13:47:38 (KST)

Message Text:
xxxx
```

- Group name and author name are **clickable hyperlinks**
- Time is always in **Korea Standard Time (KST)**
- No "VIEW GROUP" preview cards
- Join/leave service messages in the target group are **automatically deleted**

---

## Keyword Detection

The filter uses a **two-tier system**:

### Tier 1 — Strong keywords (single match = job post)

| Language | Examples |
|----------|---------|
| 🇺🇿 Uzbek | `ish bor`, `ishchi kerak`, `vakansiya`, `arbayt`, `tekpe`, `ish haqi`, `ishga olinadi` |
| 🇷🇺 Russian | `вакансия`, `нужен работник`, `подработка`, `трудоустройство` |
| 🇰🇷 Korean | `알바`, `구인`, `채용`, `시급`, `월급`, `구합니다` |

### Tier 2 — Word combinations (both words must appear anywhere in the message)

| Combo | Example message caught |
|-------|----------------------|
| `kerak` + person word | `"1 yigit kerak bugun zavod"` |
| `ish` + location word | `"zavod uchun ish bor"` |
| `работа` + context word | `"срочно работа есть склад"` |

### Testing keywords

Use the **🔍 Test Keyword** button in the admin bot — paste any message and get instant feedback showing which tier matched, which keywords triggered, and a confidence score.

---

## Running as a Service (Linux)

To keep the bot running after you close the terminal, create a systemd service:

**`/etc/systemd/system/korea-ish-bot.service`**

```ini
[Unit]
Description=Korea Ish Elonlari Bot
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User=youruser
WorkingDirectory=/path/to/telegram_job_bot
ExecStart=/path/to/venv/bin/python main.py
Restart=always
RestartSec=10
StandardOutput=journal
StandardError=journal

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```

```bash
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable korea-ish-bot
sudo systemctl start korea-ish-bot
sudo systemctl status korea-ish-bot

# View live logs
sudo journalctl -u korea-ish-bot -f
```

