## FAQ & Troubleshooting

**Q: The bot starts but no messages are being forwarded.**

Check in order:

1. Run `python main.py` and look for `✅ JOB DETECTED` in the logs
2. If you only see `MSG RECEIVED` but no detection — the messages don't contain job keywords. Use 🔍 **Test Keyword** to verify
3. If you see no `MSG RECEIVED` at all — the monitor account is not a member of the source groups
4. Use 🧪 **Test Send** to confirm the target group connection works

**Q: I get `Bad Request: message is too long` in /listgroups.**

This is handled automatically — the list is paginated into chunks of ~3800 characters. If it still happens, restart the bot with the latest `admin_bot.py`.

**Q: Join/leave messages being deleted.**

The personal Telegram account running the monitor must be an **admin** in the target group with the **"Delete messages"** permission enabled.

**Q: The same job post appears twice in the target group.**

This is the repost deduplication feature. Make sure you are running the latest `monitor.py` — it checks the `fwd_from` header of forwarded messages.

**Q: I want to add a keyword that isn't in the list.**

Open `bot/filters.py` and add it to the appropriate list in `STRONG_KEYWORDS`. Restart `main.py` for the change to take effect.

**Q: Can I run this on a VPS / cloud server?**

Yes. The recommended setup is a Linux VPS running the systemd service above. Any cloud provider works (DigitalOcean, Hetzner, AWS, etc.). The bot uses very little CPU and RAM.

---

## Security Notes

- Never commit your `.env` file — it contains your personal Telegram credentials
- The `sessions/` folder contains the Telethon session file — treat it like a password
- The admin bot only responds to your `ADMIN_USER_ID` — all other users are rejected
- Add `.env`, `sessions/`, `data/`, and `logs/` to `.gitignore` (already included)

